//? Title: Measure Grappler constant folding and CPU XLA fusion
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en

\abstract(
Compare the same elementwise GraphDef in baseline, Grappler, and XLA
sessions. Inspect the executed partition graphs and measure steady-state
latency after warm-up.
)
\toc

> A shared graph and three execution policies

The bundled GraphDef implements the upstream elementwise workload on
65,536 Float32 values. It computes \(s = 1.25\times0.5\),
\(v=s x+0.15\) and \(w=\sin(v)+\cos(x)\), then returns
\(\exp(-v^2)(w^2+0.125)\). Fetching the scalar product along with the
vector makes its replacement by a constant visible in the partition graph.

Grappler can evaluate the product of two constants before execution and
replace that multiplication with a Const node. XLA can compile several
elementwise operations into a single executable, reducing intermediate
materialization. The report scans the executed graph for the folded
node and an XLA executable. It also checks the full vector against a
double-precision scalar reference.

Build Datamunge with `-DDATAMUNGE_ENABLE_TENSORFLOW=ON` and set
`CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH` to a TensorFlow C++ SDK with CPU XLA support. The
program enables CPU JIT for its own process. The first timing includes
partition inspection and any first-run compilation. Steady timings are
the median of 30 calls after four warm-ups. Each call includes the
Datamunge-to-TensorFlow input and output copies.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <chrono>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>

int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  using Clock = std::chrono::steady_clock;
  if (!n::saved_model_runtime_available()) {
    std::println("Graph optimization requires DATAMUNGE_ENABLE_TENSORFLOW.");
    return 0;
  }
  n::enable_tensorflow_cpu_jit();
  constexpr int size = 65536;
  std::vector<float> input(size);
  for (int i = 0; i < size; ++i)
    input[i] = (i % 509 - 254) / 120.f;
  const n::NamedTensors feeds{{"features", n::from_vector(input)}};
  const std::vector<std::string> fetches{"output", "static_product"};
  constexpr std::array modes{n::GraphOptimization::Baseline, n::GraphOptimization::Grappler,
                             n::GraphOptimization::Xla};
  constexpr std::array labels{"Baseline", "Grappler", "XLA"};
  std::vector<double> medians;
  std::println("| Policy | Partition nodes | Folded | XLA | Maximum error | First run ms | Steady median µs |");
  std::println("| :--- | ---: | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |");
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < modes.size(); ++i) {
    const n::GraphSession session("fixtures/elementwise_graph.pb", modes[i]);
    std::vector<std::pair<std::string, std::string>> partition;
    const auto start = Clock::now();
    const auto result = session.run(feeds, fetches, &partition);
    const auto first = std::chrono::duration<double, std::milli>(Clock::now() - start).count();
    const bool folded = std::ranges::any_of(partition, [](const auto& node) {
      return node.first == "static_product" && node.second == "Const";
    });
    const bool xla = std::ranges::any_of(partition, [](const auto& node) {
      return node.second == "_XlaRun" || node.second == "XlaLaunch";
    });
    if (result.size() != 2 || result[0].second.shape() != n::Shape{size} ||
        result[1].second.item() != .625 || folded != (i > 0) || xla != (i == 2))
      throw std::runtime_error("Unexpected partition graph or result shape");
    const auto values = result[0].second.to_vector<float>();
    double error = 0.;
    for (int j = 0; j < size; ++j) {
      const double x = input[j], v = .625*x + .15, wave = std::sin(v) + std::cos(x);
      const double exact = std::exp(-v*v)*(wave*wave + .125);
      if (!std::isfinite(values[j])) throw std::runtime_error("Nonfinite graph output");
      error = std::max(error, std::abs(values[j] - exact));
    }
    if (error >= 3e-6) throw std::runtime_error("Graph output disagrees with the reference");

    for (int j = 0; j < 4; ++j) (void)session.run(feeds, fetches);
    std::array<double, 30> samples;
    for (auto& sample : samples) {
      const auto before = Clock::now();
      (void)session.run(feeds, fetches);
      sample = std::chrono::duration<double, std::micro>(Clock::now() - before).count();
    }
    std::ranges::sort(samples);
    medians.push_back((samples[14] + samples[15]) * .5);
    std::println("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.3g} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} |",
                 labels[i], partition.size(), folded, xla, error, first, medians.back());
  }

  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.points({1., 2., 3.}, medians, "Steady median", {37, 99, 235}, 6)
      .title("Steady CPU latency after four warm-up calls")
      .x_label("1 Baseline · 2 Grappler · 3 XLA").y_label("Microseconds")
      .save_svg("build/graph_optimization.svg");
  std::filesystem::copy_file("build/graph_optimization.svg", "figures/graph_optimization.svg",
                             std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::println("");
  std::println("\\image(figures/graph_optimization.svg)");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Policy | Partition nodes | Folded | XLA | Maximum error | First run ms | Steady median µs |
| :--- | ---: | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Baseline | 18 | false | false | 2.56e-07 | 17.3 | 205.9 |
| Grappler | 16 | true | false | 2.56e-07 | 6.8 | 166.7 |
| XLA | 6 | true | true | 2.51e-07 | 86.3 | 302.4 |

\image(figures/graph_optimization.svg)
// result_end

The partition checks establish which optimization ran. Timings depend on
the host and runtime build, and the first-run and steady-state columns
measure different phases of execution.

> References

- [TensorFlow graph optimization|https://www.tensorflow.org/guide/graph_optimization].
